From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:59:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lockscreen: Show what the PAM modules say after a wrong
 pattern

Plinius: wrong patterns now count with plinius-pinguard like wrong PINs.
After a wrong pattern the lock screen showed "Wrong Pattern" and two
seconds later "Draw Pattern" again, also while a wait ran in which no
pattern is checked. Like for the PIN (0013) it now shows what the PAM
modules said, e.g. "Wrong pattern. Next try in 30 seconds." or "Too many
wrong tries. Next try in 5 minutes.", and keeps it in view.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/lockscreen.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/lockscreen.c b/src/lockscreen.c
index b51f0ed2..ec2a150c 100644
--- a/src/lockscreen.c
+++ b/src/lockscreen.c
@@ -503,10 +503,15 @@ on_auth_authenticate_ready (GObject *source_object, GAsyncResult *result, gpoint
   if (authenticated) {
     g_signal_emit (self, signals[LOCKSCREEN_UNLOCK], 0);
   } else if (priv->pattern_mode) {
-    phosh_lockscreen_set_unlock_status (self, g_dgettext (PLINIUS_DOMAIN, "Wrong Pattern"));
+    /* Plinius: what the PAM modules said, e.g. the wait after too many wrong tries */
+    const char *message = phosh_auth_get_message (auth);
+
+    phosh_lockscreen_set_unlock_status (self, message ? message : g_dgettext (PLINIUS_DOMAIN, "Wrong Pattern"));
     phosh_pattern_pad_show_error (PHOSH_PATTERN_PAD (priv->pattern_pad));
     g_clear_handle_id (&priv->pattern_status_id, g_source_remove);
-    priv->pattern_status_id = g_timeout_add_seconds (PATTERN_STATUS_SECONDS, restore_pattern_status, self);
+    /* A wait stays in view: "Draw Pattern" would ask for tries that are not checked */
+    if (message == NULL)
+      priv->pattern_status_id = g_timeout_add_seconds (PATTERN_STATUS_SECONDS, restore_pattern_status, self);
     /* For a PIN the end of the shake animation does this (finish_shake_entry) */
     gtk_widget_set_sensitive (GTK_WIDGET (self), TRUE);
   } else {
